Normally, they are, yes. The proposal would not alter that normal
situation. It would, however, eliminate the case where, by pure luck, that
difficulty is greatly reduced.

>while Gehennom is peanuts.

Well, the effect this proposal _does_ have every game is to stiffen
Gehennom up a bit, by ensuring that although you will have the most vital
kit after the Castle wand, you won't necessarily be tooled up with every
last thing you want.

However, I think the existing difficulty curve is not bad. A tough early
game is OK, because you don't have a vast investment of time in the
character; then the game should ease off a bit, but it's OK for the
endgame to be tough because _almost_ making it is frustrating, but
interesting.

That said, I do think the middle game is too easy. If you can get to about
DL20 without serious trouble, you can scour the entire dungeon down to
Medusa and waste time on piddly optimisations without any clock on the
game at all. Something that forced you to proceed eventually would not
affect novices much, who generally burn along in packrat in-and-out mode.
